<title>USA: Candela gets FDA skin-scanning device okay.</title>
<headline>Candela gets FDA skin-scanning device okay.</headline>
<dateline>WAYLAND, Mass. 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Candela Corp said Thursday that the U.S. Food and Drug Administration has cleared a microprocessor-driven skin scanning device called Skinscan for aesthetic laser surgery.</p>
<p>Skinscan is manufactured for Candela by Fotona d.d., the Slovenia-based developer of the product.</p>
<p>Candela said it holds exclusive marketing and distribution rights for these products in the United States, Far East, South America, as well as some European and African countries.</p>
